    "The previous scan of %@ is kept when you rescan. Scan again later and this view shows what grew and what shrank in between." : {
      "comment" : "Disk Map (1.6.0)",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der vorherige Scan von %@ bleibt beim erneuten Scannen erhalten. Scanne später noch einmal, und diese Ansicht zeigt, was in der Zwischenzeit gewachsen und was geschrumpft ist."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The previous scan of %@ is kept when you rescan. Scan again later and this view shows what grew and what shrank in between."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L'analyse précédente de %@ est conservée quand vous analysez à nouveau. Relancez l'analyse plus tard et cette vue montrera ce qui a grossi et ce qui a rétréci entre-temps."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "重新扫描时会保留%@的上一次扫描。之后再次扫描，此视图会显示这段时间内增大和减小的内容。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The range contains %1$d addresses. Choose %2$d or fewer." : {
      "comment" : "Identity entries: English renders the key verbatim. Present so the two tables mirror each other and English copy stays auditable in one place; check-localization.py enforces the parity.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Bereich enthält %1$d Adressen. Wähle %2$d oder weniger."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The range contains %1$d addresses. Choose %2$d or fewer."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La plage contient %1$d adresses. Choisissez-en %2$d ou moins."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "该范围包含 %1$d 个地址，请选择 %2$d 个或更少。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The run-queue length (roughly how many processes are competing to run) averaged over the last minute, with the 5 and 15-minute figures beside it. A load near your core count (%@) means the CPU is fully subscribed; well above it means work is queuing." : {
      "comment" : "Metric Cards & Explanations",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Länge der Run-Queue (ungefähr, wie viele Prozesse um Rechenzeit konkurrieren), gemittelt über die letzte Minute, daneben die Werte für 5 und 15 Minuten. Eine Last nahe deiner Kernanzahl (%@) bedeutet, dass die CPU voll ausgelastet ist; deutlich darüber heißt, dass Arbeit wartet."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The run-queue length (roughly how many processes are competing to run) averaged over the last minute, with the 5 and 15-minute figures beside it. A load near your core count (%@) means the CPU is fully subscribed; well above it means work is queuing."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La longueur de la file d'exécution (en gros, combien de processus se disputent le CPU), en moyenne sur la dernière minute, avec les valeurs à 5 et 15 minutes à côté. Une charge proche de votre nombre de cœurs (%@) signifie que le CPU est pleinement sollicité ; bien au-dessus, le travail fait la queue."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "运行队列长度（大致代表有多少进程在竞争运行），在过去 1 分钟内的平均值，旁边附带 5 分钟和 15 分钟的数值。接近核心数的负载 (%@) 意味着 CPU 已被充分利用；远高于核心数则意味着任务正在排队。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
